    "turn_text": "bet. In my O&C bill, the issue presented because the federal government owns boats to our land, I have proposed doubling the harvest on average each year for the next 50 years. And I talked with Ryan Zinke, the Secretary of Interior about it here recently, and I hope to be supportive of it. And I can't believe that we can get that harvest up in a sustainable way while protecting our treasures or screens, and by the way, the screens and the wilderness areas have made respiration a major jobs magnet. For this state, recreation has become a big, big industry for work. I think, again, if we have sensible policies, and we don't have fires burning all those areas up. We're going to continue to be able to build on that.",
