    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/3/73207.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 45,
    "turn_text": "Well, everybody wants to talk about who won and who lost. And I was very heavily involved in that package as well, particularly with the debt ceiling provisions, which goes to the Senate Finance Committee. I was working very closely with the Senator Schumer and the leadership in terms of getting that right because that represents something central to maintaining our image that we have our fiscal house and orders that we pay our bills. I was heavily involved in that. And people are now asking, well, who won? Did the Democrats win? I'll tell you, who wins? When you keep the government open, you don't fund matters like the wall or something like that, or going to tell me they want to build roads, not walls. And I think America and Oregon won in that deal. And I don't want to talk about it in terms of Democrats or",
